{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what happened that brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, doctor. I fell two days ago. My boyfriend asked me to sit on his lap, and when I stood up, I just lost balance and fell. I hit my head, shoulder, and leg. My son caught me before I hit the floor hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Did you feel dizzy or lightheaded before the fall? Any chest pain, shortness of breath, or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. I didn’t pass out or feel faint. But I’ve been feeling unsteady on my feet for a while now. I’ve had a few falls before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. You mentioned you were using a cane—what happened to it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I lost it a few weeks ago. I’ve been meaning to get another, but I haven’t had the chance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ve done some tests. Your CT scan of the head is normal—no bleeding or stroke. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also did an EKG and checked your heart enzymes. Everything looks stable—no signs of a heart attack or dangerous rhythm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had heart surgery before—CABG—so I always worry about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see that in your history. You’re on Plavix and aspirin, which we’ll continue. We also checked your blood pressure when you stood up—no big drop—so it’s not a blood pressure issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why do I keep feeling off balance?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It seems to be chronic instability. The CT did show some chronic changes in your brain’s white matter, likely from small vessel disease—common with high blood pressure and diabetes. But nothing new or dangerous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have diabetes, yes. It’s been hard to keep under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar came in at 255, and we’ve been monitoring it. It’s been running high—mostly in the 200s. Your A1c was 8.5%, which tells us sugars have been elevated over the last few months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I haven’t been taking my insulin the same every day. Sometimes I forget, or I don’t go to the day program where they help me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay—we’re going to help you with that. We’re changing your insulin to a simpler plan: one type, twice a day—25 units in the morning, 15 at dinner. Plus a sliding scale if your sugar goes over 200."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds easier. Will that help me feel better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, better sugar control can improve energy and may help with overall stability. We also checked your thyroid and calcium levels—both normal—so no other cause for the weakness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my shoulder and back? They’re sore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have a big bruise on your shoulder and tenderness in your upper back, but the X-ray showed no fractures. It’s a contusion—just soft tissue injury. We can give you pain medicine if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like something for the shoulder pain, please."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ll order naproxen for you—take it with food to protect your stomach. And we’ll make sure your other medications are continued—like your blood pressure, cholesterol, and asthma meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I take a lot of pills—I sometimes get confused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2179-09-30 21:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. That’s why going to the day program regularly can help. They can make sure you get the right doses at the right times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, doctor. My shoulder still hurts, but the medicine helps. I’m just worried about falling again when I go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a valid concern. Physical therapy saw you this morning. They recommend you use a cane and get a home safety evaluation—like removing loose rugs or adding grab bars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can do that. Will I need therapy after I leave?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re setting up outpatient physical therapy to work on your strength and balance. The cane will help you stay steady in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes me feel better. What about my blood pressure and cholesterol? Are those okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been stable. We held one of your water pills briefly when you came in, in case you were dehydrated, but we’ve restarted it. Your cholesterol meds are continuing—your last level was high, so it’s important to stay on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my new insulin—how do I start that at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take 25 units in the morning and 15 at dinner, under the skin. We’ll give you a sliding scale—if your sugar is over 200, you’ll take extra based on the chart we’ll provide."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I should go to the day program every day to make sure I take it right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2179-10-01 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That will help a lot. We’ll also send instructions to your primary doctor for follow-up in a week or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2179-10-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2179-10-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling okay. A little sore, but ready to go home. Just nervous about falling again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2179-10-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve set you up with a cane, outpatient physical therapy, and a home safety check. Plus your new insulin plan should help you feel stronger over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2179-10-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I’ll try to go to the day program more often and take my insulin like I’m supposed to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2179-10-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we can ask. Take care, and call your doctor if you have any concerns—especially if you fall again or your sugars are too high or low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2179-10-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2179-09-30 21:06:00",
    "admission_end": "2179-10-02 17:53:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 60-year-old woman with a history of coronary artery disease, prior CABG, type 2 diabetes, hypertension, and a previous stroke was admitted after a mechanical fall at home two days prior. She reported no loss of consciousness or pre-syncopal symptoms but described chronic dizziness and gait instability. Evaluation included a normal head CT and EKG, negative cardiac enzymes, and no orthostatic hypotension, ruling out acute neurological or cardiac causes. She was found to have contusions to the head, shoulder, and leg but no fractures. Physical therapy recommended a cane and outpatient rehabilitation for balance and strength. Her diabetes was poorly controlled with admission glucose in the 200s and a recent A1c of 8.5%; her insulin regimen was simplified to 70/30 insulin twice daily with sliding scale coverage. She was discharged home with instructions to use a cane, attend physical therapy, adhere to her new insulin regimen, and follow up with her primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Syncope and collapse",
      "Contusion of back",
      "Contusion of unspecified part of lower limb",
      "Fall from other slipping, tripping, or stumbling",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status",
      "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty status",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Personal history of transient ischemic attack (TIA), and cerebral infarction without residual deficits",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Bell's palsy",
      "Stress incontinence, female",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Lichenification and lichen simplex chronicus"
    ]
  }
}
